Subject: [PATCH] docs(brainstorms): audit split spike: the engine removes
 sensitive data, the sink renders (R22)

Answers the question raised on 2026-10-05 of whether headers and other
sensitive values should be removed before they reach an audit sink or by
the sink. R22 puts removal in the engine, before the record exists, so
the rule is uniform across sinks and sits inside the hashed bytes; drops
or keyed-digests rather than masks; and marks what was removed so a
consumer can tell redacted from never present. AE10 pins it, a key
decision records why, and an outstanding question carries the
operator-facing shape to planning.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Leva <120221487+Levaj2000@users.noreply.github.com>
